Needs a live SurrealDB: the `bakery-surreal` datasource auto-connects on
startup, so without one the app logs a connect ERROR and the shared "clean
startup" check fails. The published-binary BDD runner has no database.

Run it explicitly against a local instance:
  surreal start --user root --pass root
  python3 apps/bakery/seed.py
  cargo run -p test-framework -- apps/bakery

Until this app carried the surreal catalog it was the suite's only fully
offline example; `faker-demo` is now the one app that starts with no external
dependency at all, so keep that one runnable in CI.
